# Technical documentation: {{ .Product.Name }}

The technical documentation the EU Cyber Resilience Act asks for (Article 31, Annex VII). Point numbers follow the
annex. Keep it, and the EU declaration of conformity, at the disposal of market surveillance authorities for at least
ten years after the product is placed on the market, or for the support period if that is longer (Article 13(13)).

## 1. General description

- **Intended purpose**: {{ or .Product.Purpose "TODO: the intended purpose (`product.purpose` in shipward.yaml)." }}
- **Versions**: TODO: the software versions that affect conformity with the essential requirements.
- **Information for users**: [user-information.md](user-information.md).
- **Product class**: {{ template "class" .Product.Class }}

  Check the product against the categories of Annex III and Annex IV. The technical descriptions of the categories
  are in Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2025/2392
  (<https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX:32025R2392>). A product is in an Annex III category
  when it has the core functionality of that category (Article 7(1)).

  - Annex III, class I (`important-1`): identity management and privileged access management software and
    hardware; standalone and embedded browsers; password managers; software that searches for, removes or
    quarantines malicious software; VPN products; network management systems; SIEM systems; boot managers; public
    key infrastructure and digital certificate issuance software; physical and virtual network interfaces; operating
    systems; routers, modems for the internet, and switches; microprocessors, microcontrollers, ASICs and FPGAs with
    security-related functionalities; smart home general purpose virtual assistants; smart home products with
    security functionalities; internet-connected toys covered by Directive 2009/48/EC that have social interactive
    features (for example speaking or filming) or location tracking features; personal wearable products worn or
    placed on a human body that have a health monitoring purpose and to which Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU)
    2017/746 do not apply (a product those apply to is outside the CRA, Article 2(2)), or personal wearable products
    intended for use by and for children.
  - Annex III, class II (`important-2`): hypervisors and container runtime systems; firewalls, intrusion detection
    and prevention systems; tamper-resistant microprocessors and microcontrollers.
  - Annex IV (`critical`): hardware devices with security boxes; smart meter gateways and other devices for advanced
    security purposes; smartcards or similar devices, including secure elements.
  - None of these (`default`).

